{"tool_name":"shasta","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"shasta","identifiers":[],"license":"MIT","summary":"Rapidly produce accurate assembled sequence using as input DNA reads generated by Oxford Nanopore flow cells.","home_url":"https://github.com/chanzuckerberg/shasta","keywords":["Genomics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":579},"biotools":{"id":"shasta","home":"https://github.com/paoloshasta/shasta","license":"MIT","summary":"De novo assembly from Oxford Nanopore reads.","addition_date":"2022-03-20T16:23:19.118930Z","last_update_date":"2022-03-20T16:23:19.122746Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Suite"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:shasta","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Benedict Paten"},{"name":"Kishwar Shafin"},{"name":"Marina Haukness"},{"name":"Miten Jain"},{"name":"Paolo Carnevali"},{"name":"Ryan Lorig-Roach"},{"name":"Trevor Pesout"}],"documentation":[{"type":["Code of conduct"],"url":"https://github.com/chanzuckerberg/.github/blob/master/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md"},{"type":["General"],"url":"https://chanzuckerberg.github.io/shasta/"},{"type":["Quick start guide"],"url":"https://chanzuckerberg.github.io/shasta/QuickStart.html"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0925"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Genome assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0525"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0925"},"format":[{"term":"FASTQ","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1930"}]}]}],"name":"Shasta","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41587-020-0503-6","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020, The Author(s).De novo assembly of a human genome using nanopore long-read sequences has been reported, but it used more than 150,000 CPU hours and weeks of wall-clock time. To enable rapid human genome assembly, we present Shasta, a de novo long-read assembler, and polishing algorithms named MarginPolish and HELEN. Using a single PromethION nanopore sequencer and our toolkit, we assembled 11 highly contiguous human genomes de novo in 9 d. We achieved roughly 63\u00d7 coverage, 42-kb read N50 values and 6.5\u00d7 coverage in reads >100 kb using three flow cells per sample. Shasta produced a complete haploid human genome assembly in under 6 h on a single commercial compute node. MarginPolish and HELEN polished haploid assemblies to more than 99.9% identity (Phred quality score QV = 30) with nanopore reads alone. Addition of proximity-ligation sequencing enabled near chromosome-level scaffolds for all 11 genomes. We compare our assembly performance to existing methods for diploid, haploid and trio-binned human samples and report superior accuracy and speed.","authors":[{"name":"Akeson M."},{"name":"Armstrong J."},{"name":"Bosworth C."},{"name":"Carnevali P."},{"name":"Costa V."},{"name":"Eichler E.E."},{"name":"Garrison E."},{"name":"Green R.E."},{"name":"Haukness M."},{"name":"Haussler D."},{"name":"Jain M."},{"name":"Kilburn D."},{"name":"Koren S."},{"name":"Liu K.J."},{"name":"Lorig-Roach R."},{"name":"Marschall T."},{"name":"Maurer N."},{"name":"Mayes S."},{"name":"Miga K.H."},{"name":"Monlong J."},{"name":"Munson K.M."},{"name":"Olsen H.E."},{"name":"Paten B."},{"name":"Pesout T."},{"name":"Phillippy A."},{"name":"Salama S."},{"name":"Sedlazeck F.J."},{"name":"Shafin K."},{"name":"Sorensen M."},{"name":"Tigyi K."},{"name":"Vollger M.R."},{"name":"Zook J.M."}],"citationCount":84,"date":"2020-09-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Biotechnology","title":"Nanopore sequencing and the Shasta toolkit enable efficient de novo assembly of eleven human genomes"},"pmcid":"PMC7483855","pmid":"32686750"}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"ter